    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The contested amount is the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-02748, charged at 19:15:27 and still standing on the ledger (EV-FARE-02748). I am refunding it in full to the rider, and the driver receives nothing.\n\nWhy the charge cannot stand. Under POL-NS-01 a no-show fee is chargeable only if all four conditions hold. Three do: (a) the trip record (EV-TRIP-02748) carries a driver 'arrived' event at 19:11:48; (b) the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02748) places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 19:11:48, the first qualifying in-geofence fix; and (c) he held position inside that geofence continuously for 200 seconds, from 19:11:48 to 19:15:08, which exceeds the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180). Condition (d) fails on the driver's own record: he terminated the trip with cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, and POL-NS-01 expressly excludes that code from the three that satisfy limb (d). The driver concedes this. Where the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius — as they do here, his minimum distance to the pin being 0.44 m — POL-NS-01 fixes the outcome: the fee is not chargeable, the rider is refunded the SGD 4.50 in full, and no driver compensation is payable. The mis-selected reason code goes into the referrals as a driver-education item.\n\nThe rider is independently exonerated under POL-NS-04. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02748) shows the rider sent a locating message ('at the lift lobby') at 19:12:48; the driver posted no reply in the 120 seconds that followed and made no in-app call (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty); and the rider's own device sat within the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius on all 40 qualifying fixes, 12.5–19.7 m from the pin throughout. Both routes give the same result: full refund of the SGD 4.50, no compensation.\n\nOn the driver's claim for SGD 3.60 compensation: the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 1, below the 4-or-more limb; 1/137 = 0.007, below the 0.08 rate limb), but POL-NS-07 pays compensation only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not. Compensation is therefore refused. There is no goodwill payment either: POL-NS-03(ii) applies only where the driver's stationary fixes lie outside the arrival radius (within 400 m), and here they were inside it, so POL-NS-03 does not apply at all.\n\nOn the rider's POL-NS-06 argument (200-second dwell against a 300-second minimum): rejected. The 300-second figure in fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec is retained only to interpret records authored before policy version 2 and is never applied to a record that carries platform_policy; the free waiting period in force is 180 seconds, and the 200-second dwell exceeds it. The derived block's −20-second 'shortfall' is in fact a 20-second surplus against 180 seconds. POL-NS-06 does not apply. The arrival marker is also not false under POL-NS-05 — the driver was at the pin (0.44 m) and stationary at 0.0 kph, so neither the 300 m nor the 15 kph trigger is engaged, and no false-arrival referral arises.\n\nIntegrity and confidence. Every artifact this ruling rests on — EV-GPS-02748, EV-TRIP-02748, EV-CHAT-02748 and EV-FARE-02748 — is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0. There is no clock skew (the arrival event matches the first in-geofence fix to the second), no trace defect (100% coverage, 10-second cadence, zero gaps, both tracks present), no chat defect (2 messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count), and the fare line reconciles exactly to the SGD 4.50 net fee, so there is no POL-NS-08 defect and no POL-NS-09 escalation. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02748-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); nothing in this ruling rests on it — POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is both unavailable and unnecessary, because there is a single continuous in-geofence run — so I record it, note it carries no deciding fact, and it does not cap confidence. Confidence is 0.95.\n\nThe monetary effect is SGD 4.50, which does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue. Both parties may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
